 "notes": "Screen-then-choose biomedical alloy paper: tensile screen (z15) motivates DES/down_select z16, which carries the rest. PACKET ANOMALY: paper Fig. 5 (micro-CT, BV/TV) is missing; packet F5 = paper Fig. 6 (histology), F6 = Fig. 7 (EDS), F7 = Fig. 8 (systemic). F2 and F4 captions are garbled. F3, F6, F7 not opened (budget); their OBS carry figs=[] and fig_ref. Audits: z14 (binary Zn0.8Li is more ductile, harder, higher YS: 'best mechanical properties' is UTS only; qualifies the down-select), z29 (osteogenic gain falls with extract concentration; 100% is cytotoxic: qualifies the ion-release MEC), z37 (one 24 w section shows a fragmented scaffold: qualifies load-bearing suitability). Load-bearing qualification z42 is argued from tensile values; no in-vivo mechanical test. In vivo degradation z39 typed PRP chemical_corrosion (v03 rule).",
